take a break  if you find yourself stuck on something  if you find yourself unable to make  progress on a project that you're  working on  take a break  because often if you just try to ram  something through you're not going to  get the results that you're looking for  and if you take 10 minutes  go away from it and come back  you'll often be refreshed and be able to  solve the problem  the two quick stories for you that  happened to me recently so  yesterday jason who's helping me with my  new website and all the branding that  goes with it he's working on some coding  problems something on the website some  some bug that he's trying to work  through and he couldn't find a solution  and he's spending like an hour on this  thing and and i just see him on the  computer like uh rubbing his eyes and  unable to make progress on this thing  and so  he does a smart thing and he goes and he  takes a break  he goes out goes for a walk gets some  food comes back and within five minutes  of sitting down again he solves it  and this happens to me  so much and i don't know what it is  about the human condition that that that  allows us to to do this but i often find  myself with these kinds of problems and  and i may come back to it the same day  or maybe it's the next day but the  solution often comes really quickly  after taking a break so again if you  find yourself pounding away on something  and you're just not making progress you  just can't figure out what the problem  is  take a break even like 10-15 minutes and  come back to it another quick example is  uh in salsa dancing  i love salsa dancing i love teaching  people how to dance as well and i was  working with a student  teaching her how to do some turns  and  she just wasn't getting it  and so i said okay you know what it's  okay it's okay we'll come back to it  we'll move on to other stuff and it was  it was an hour that was with her  and we did other moves and at the end of  the hour came back and did the turn  a